"""allm_workspaces.py — AnythingLLM workspace registry + determination.

Atlas registers AnythingLLM workspaces as nodes (allm:<slug>), but a
name tag is not management. This module is the determination layer
(Brian, 2026-10-22): it says what each workspace is FOR, who owns it,
what lands in it, and — for new material — WHERE it goes and why.

Brian's determination rules, encoded:
  R1. A workspace is one domain of questions owned by one part of
      the ecosystem (a business line, desk, project, or person-matter).
  R2. Separation is PER BUSINESS, never per category: "keep Zilara
      details separate even though both are MLMs" (Brian, 2026-10-22).
      A shared category (e.g. MLM) is NEVER a reason to route material
      into a sibling business's workspace.
  R3. All data about a business lives in that business's workspace:
      "Oliabo is a workspace we need to store all data Oliabo"
      (Brian, 2026-10-22) — regardless of which desk produced it.
  R4. unsorted is an intake tray, not a home; quarantine holds
      untrusted content and never mixes with trusted bodies.
  R5. New workspace only when: no existing workspace's owner covers
      the subject AND the subject is a named owner in its own right.
      Otherwise the material goes to the owning workspace, or to
      unsorted until an owner is determined.
  R6. Every MLM business Brian is ACTIVELY BUILDING has its own
      workspace (Brian, 2026-10-22). The active list is Brian's
      (2026-10-21: exactly three — Zilara, GotBackup, Vate Life);
      audit() flags any active MLM lacking a workspace. Businesses
      not on the active list get no workspace from this rule —
      Oliabo's rests on its own ruling (R3), and names that merely
      appear in campaign data (Sipology, LiveGood, le-Vel, ...)
      get nothing until Brian designates them active.
  R7. Every MARKETING SKIN has its own workspace (Brian,
      2026-10-22: 'TrafficStreemz needs its own workspace. Also
      AegeanVedaFlow, CryptoStreemz — each marketing skin needs
      its own anythingllm workspace'). Skins on record:
      TrafficStreemz (already live), AegeanVedaFlow,
      CryptoStreemz. A skin's workspace holds the SKIN's material
      (its offers, bundles, campaigns); business details still
      live in each business's own workspace (R2/R3).
  R8. THE NEGATIVE REGISTRY (Brian, 2026-10-22): builds Brian is
      intentionally NOT building get a workspace of their own —
      'builds-we-are-not-building' — holding the WHY of each
      rejection: the evidence, the mechanism, and what would have
      to change to reopen it. It is the mirror of the build_zones
      'why' (why chosen builds ARE built). determine() checks the
      NOT_BUILDING list FIRST: material about a rejected build
      routes to the negative registry, never to a builds body —
      so no dead end is re-researched or quietly revived.
      First citizen: Epyc 7001 — 'we are not building epyc 7001;
      i am intentionally not building that one' (Brian).
  R9. COACHING BODIES ARE PER AUDIENCE (Brian, 2026-10-22: 'we
      need an anythingllm workspace to put all the AI Strategies
      that I am planning to coach to Network Marketers; and
      another ... to coach to other users of successbrian os').
      The AI strategies Brian teaches live in one workspace PER
      COACHED AUDIENCE — never one merged 'AI strategies' pile:
      what he teaches a network marketer is framed, priced, and
      sequenced differently from what he teaches a fellow
      SuccessBrian OS operator. Audiences on record:
      network-marketers, sbos-users.
  R10. COMPETITIVE RESEARCH IS ITS OWN BODY, sibling to the
      domain it studies — it holds what OTHERS are doing, never
      Brian's own material (first instance ruled by Brian,
      2026-10-22: 'ai-strategies-competitive-research — where
      we hold ideas of what other influencers and coaches are
      promoting'). Research organizes by the market/question;
      R2's separation protects Brian's own businesses, it does
      not scatter his intel. Further research bodies from the
      2026-10-22 ideas slate (Health MLM, Systeme.io, Blood
      Sugar Systems) remain IDEAS until Brian designates them.
  R11. SPACES FOLLOW AUDIENCES (Brian, 2026-10-22: 'every
      audience we are trying to build gets a space; and in
      many cases a competitive research one to store the other
      stuff'). The general law R6/R7/R9 converge on: once an
      audience is being built, it gets its own space — the
      SPACE is mandatory; a competitive-research sibling is
      common but ruled per audience, never automatic. audit()
      enforces space coverage for every audience on record
      and reports each audience still lacking a research body
      as a standing question, not a violation.
  R12. PROJECTS AND BLOGS GET SPACES TOO (Brian, 2026-10-22:
      'all of our vibe coded projects need their own
      anythingllm workspace; when appropriate, we need
      workspaces for competitive research; we need spaces for
      each blog; we need spaces for blog niche competitive
      research (where appropriate)'). (a) Every vibe-coded
      project on the PROJECTS list has its own workspace —
      the list is Brian's, extended by designation; a
      directory on a disk is not automatically a project.
