      little, look at the bottom a little (the oldest
      tasks that aren't completed)... basically looking
      at all sides of the process and keep pushing
      everything to the middle'). The board's attention
      is stratified: pending gates and the newest
      arrivals (the top), the oldest uncompleted tasks
      (the bottom — nothing starves at the end of the
      queue), and the mass between. Every session
      samples all sides; the direction of everything is
      the middle — ruled, resolved, done. queue_watch.py
      is the instrument: strata, ages, starvation flags,
      and the session's suggested pull order.
