      must learn how to make better and better
      suggestions over time'). A suggestion is a
      tracked claim, not a moment: board_learning.py
      keeps the ledger — suggestion (seat, item, gate
      score) -> executive decision (accepted /
      modified / rejected, per R35) -> outcome
      (worked / failed / mixed). Per-seat scorecards
      and calibration feed the next session's brief:
      a seat whose high-scored suggestions keep
      getting rejected is miscalibrated, and the brief
      says so in plain words. The board's memory is
      the ledger — without outcomes recorded there is
      no learning, only repetition.
